CORE
main.c
--generate-function-body make_l1 --generate-function-body-options havoc --max-dynamic-object-instances 10
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
nondet initialisation reached the limit of 10 dynamic objects
make_l1::malloc_site\$8
--
^warning: ignoring
^\*\*\*\* WARNING: no body for function
make_l1::malloc_site\$9
--
--max-dynamic-object-instances limits the number of objects allocated when
generating a havocking body for a function returning a pointer into a deep
struct hierarchy.  The hierarchy allocates 341 objects without a limit; with a
limit of 10, only 10 allocation sites are emitted, so make_l1::malloc_site$8 is
the last one present and make_l1::malloc_site$9 is absent.  The indices depend
on the object factory's numbering of fresh symbols.
